out so we're gonna test that

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:08.790
in comparison to the Mavic Pro Platinum,

00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:12.700
the DJI Spark and the
Phantom 4 Pro Advanced.

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:13.810
And here's our little Mavic Air.

00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:15.370
My precious.

00:00:15.370 --> 00:00:16.270
I've never even seen that movie,

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:17.740
so I don't even get the reference.

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:19.010
So right now I'm updating one of the apps

00:00:19.010 --> 00:00:21.535
before we go and then
we're gonna start flying.

00:00:21.535 --> 00:00:23.770
♪ I got two phones. ♪

00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:25.236
One for my friends, one for my drone.

00:00:25.236 --> 00:00:26.622
(laughs)

00:00:26.622 --> 00:00:29.205
(upbeat music)

00:00:34.292 --> 00:00:35.610
We've got all four of our drones lined up.

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:36.560
We're gonna do a quick little test.

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:38.900
Basically just getting a
nice little camera view here

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:40.050
without anything moving.

00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:41.880
I do have to shoot the Spark separately,

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:42.960
because it connects to Wi-Fi

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:45.120
and all of these things
are interfering with it.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:47.480
So first we'll shoot these
three, then the Spark.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.100
Hopefully, it'll sort of look the same.

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:49.933
Record.

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:51.673
Record.

00:00:51.673 --> 00:00:53.320
Phantom record.

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:54.242
Every 4K 30,

00:00:54.242 --> 00:00:55.075
4K 30.

00:00:55.075 --> 00:00:58.000
I'm gonna do a quick
little walk in front of it.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.583
(upbeat music)

00:01:23.613 --> 00:01:24.950
Hello.
- Is that what you want?

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:26.033
- [Man] Yeah.

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:29.493
Alright.

00:01:29.493 --> 00:01:32.076
(upbeat music)

00:02:00.135 --> 00:02:03.552
(moves into dance music)

00:02:15.377 --> 00:02:18.210
(blades spinning)

00:02:23.003 --> 00:02:24.660
- So we've got the Mavic
Pro Platinum out right now,

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:26.270
and one of the things
that was new about this

00:02:26.270 --> 00:02:29.040
is it supposedly is 40% quieter.

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:30.661
And listening to it now,

00:02:30.661 --> 00:02:34.149
(blades spinning)

00:02:34.149 --> 00:02:35.910
(birds squawking)

00:02:35.910 --> 00:02:38.654
It is a lot more quiet
even than the Mavic Air.

00:02:38.654 --> 00:02:41.237
(upbeat music)

00:03:29.795 --> 00:03:31.740
So after reviewing the footage
from all four of the drones,

00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:33.160
one of the things that I
was the most shocked at

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:35.150
was the variance in
color between the four.

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:36.410
I put everything on auto.

00:03:36.410 --> 00:03:38.180
Auto color balance, auto exposure,

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:39.830
pretty much everything
so that you guys can see

00:03:39.830 --> 00:03:40.990
exactly what you would be getting

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:42.300
directly out of the drones.

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:43.580
One of the things that I thought though,

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:44.480
was kind of shocking,

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:47.870
is the best auto color
came from the Spark.

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:48.950
I've even noticed differences

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:50.640
between the two of the same exact drones,

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:52.550
like my sister, we both have a Mavic Pro,

00:03:52.550 --> 00:03:55.290
and even flying those on
seemingly the same settings,

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:56.227
sometimes I will be like,

00:03:56.227 --> 00:03:58.280
"This looks different than yours."

00:03:58.280 --> 00:03:59.780
I feel like that's something
that's pretty common,

00:03:59.780 --> 00:04:01.720
but what's great is you can
pretty much customize anything.

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:03.040
So depending upon what the light is like,

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:05.340
so you can set the color balance
to match wherever you are.

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:06.970
Another cool thing that
we tried out in Malibu

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:08.720
is, Nathan was flying his Phantom 4,

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:10.750
and he added a lot onto his footage.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:12.770
So he was doing this in
camera, on the drone,

00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:14.220
so basically what I'm gonna show you now

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:15.340
is what he shot.

00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:17.350
This is right from the drone to your eyes.

00:04:17.350 --> 00:04:18.970
I am doing no color corrections.

00:04:18.970 --> 00:04:20.231
All happened within spec.

00:04:20.231 --> 00:04:23.731
(gentle electronic music)

00:04:38.223 --> 00:04:42.090
- My personal philosophy on
shutter speed for drones,

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:43.770
is that you should actually shoot

00:04:43.770 --> 00:04:45.450
with a slower shutter speed.

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:48.470
So, if you're filming
at 30 frames a second,

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:52.470
it's not a bad idea to
film at a 30th of a second.

00:04:52.470 --> 00:04:54.220
So you have to have mutual density filter.

00:04:54.220 --> 00:04:56.540
When the drone is moving through space,

00:04:56.540 --> 00:04:58.110
you're taking pictures as you shoot video.

00:04:58.110 --> 00:04:59.390
So it feels steppy.

00:04:59.390 --> 00:05:01.700
As you watch playback of a drone,

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:03.760
with a sharp shutter that's moving fast.

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:04.593
It feels like

00:05:04.593 --> 00:05:05.780
ba, ba, ba, ba, ba, ba.

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:07.727
So I started the day with my ND filter.

00:05:07.727 --> 00:05:10.810
This is the DJI, and
this is the eight filter.

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:13.510
- So far there aren't any
available yet for the Mavic Air,

00:05:13.510 --> 00:05:14.343
but I do use them

00:05:14.343 --> 00:05:15.750
when I'm flying with
my Mavic or my Phantom.

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:18.350
Especially on sunny days because
it makes a huge difference.

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:19.580
One of the things that I forgot to mention

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:20.800
on the Mavic Air review,

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:22.420
is they have two new
smart capture features.

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:23.870
They have an astroid and boomerang.

00:05:23.870 --> 00:05:27.000
So basically the drone will
do a set flight pattern

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:28.620
and they'll save that right to your phone,

00:05:28.620 --> 00:05:30.640
so you're able to share
that out immediately.

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:32.220
So I'd say that my favorite
is probably the astroid.

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:34.560
So basically the drone follows
a flight pattern directly up.

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:36.030
So it does a really cool spherical shot

00:05:36.030 --> 00:05:37.333
of everything around you.

00:05:41.183 --> 00:05:43.766
(upbeat music)

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:49.080
Also boomerang, it just takes off

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:50.740
and creates a boomerang pattern.

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:52.800
So it goes up, out, and then back directly

00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:53.795
where it started.

00:05:53.795 --> 00:05:56.378
(upbeat music)

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:20.990
So far I am loving the Mavic Air,

00:06:20.990 --> 00:06:23.680
it's amazing but the only
problem is the battery life.

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:25.160
It does only last 21 minutes

00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:27.040
which is still a fair
amount of flight time

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:28.780
but I am so used to having extra batteries

00:06:28.780 --> 00:06:30.410
and for this I only had one,

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:32.180
so I've been struggling
in shooting this video

00:06:32.180 --> 00:06:33.900
for the past like week and a half,

00:06:33.900 --> 00:06:35.430
because every time I go to film,

00:06:35.430 --> 00:06:37.440
I only have like 21
minutes until I can go back

00:06:37.440 --> 00:06:38.300
and charge the battery.

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:39.330
Right now, the sun is going down,

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:40.620
my battery is dead so,

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:42.610
whatever I shot is whatever I shot.

00:06:42.610 --> 00:06:44.240
The batteries die very, very quickly.

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:45.880
So I definitely recommend if you are going

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:47.800
to be getting this, do
get the fly more package.

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:49.900
It is worth the extra money
for the extra batteries

00:06:49.900 --> 00:06:51.600
'cause you're gonna need 'em.

